Subject: [M152] service_worker: Handle reentrant operations during job abort

Original change's description:
> service_worker: Handle reentrant operations during job abort
>
> When aborting jobs in ServiceWorkerJobCoordinator, callbacks
> triggered during job abortion (e.g. status change notifications) may
> reentrantly interact with the job coordinator (such as registering new
> jobs or modifying job queues).
>
> This CL updates JobQueue::AbortAll() to pop elements before aborting
> them and updates ServiceWorkerJobCoordinator::Abort/AbortAll/FinishJob
> to avoid holding iterators across callbacks.
>
